# CODEOWNERS: human review on Vaultex trust paths (ROADMAP §9.2, M5 exit criterion 6).
#
# @OWNER is a placeholder for the maintainer's GitHub handle(s), set once the owner answers
# Q-RUN-4 (docs/TASKS.md §3). Until then no code owner is assigned: GitHub ignores an owner
# that does not exist or has no write access to the repository.
#
# This file only names reviewers. Review is enforced once branch protection on `main` and
# `dev` turns on "Require review from Code Owners"; replace the placeholder first.
#
# How GitHub reads it: from the pull request's base branch, so a PR cannot re-route its own
# review. Patterns follow .gitignore syntax (so no `{a,b}` braces), minus `!` negation and
# `[ ]` ranges. Paths are case-sensitive. A pattern ending in `/` covers everything below
# it. The LAST matching pattern wins, so a narrower rule must sit below the broader rule it
# refines.
#
# ponytail: one owner today, so every trust area maps to the same handle. When the
# cryptographer is engaged, add them to the crypto and kernel blocks, and re-check the
# last-match order before giving any block different owners.

# Crypto: MPC protocols, Paillier and its proofs, key storage, enclave attestation,
# recovery (planned crate).
/crates/mpc-wallet-core/src/protocol/   @OWNER
/crates/mpc-wallet-core/src/paillier/   @OWNER
/crates/mpc-wallet-core/src/key_store/  @OWNER
/crates/mpc-wallet-core/src/enclave/    @OWNER
/crates/vaultex-recovery/               @OWNER

# Transport and control plane.
/crates/mpc-wallet-core/src/transport/  @OWNER
/crates/mpc-wallet-core/src/rpc/        @OWNER

# Services: MPC node, gateway, Guard, outflow monitor.
/services/                              @OWNER

# Kernel: the verifier, the contract types it decides on, and the admin and approver CLIs.
/crates/vaultex-verify/                 @OWNER
/crates/vaultex-types/                  @OWNER
/crates/vaultex-cli-admin/              @OWNER

# CI and gates: workflows, Dependabot, this file, CI scripts, the adversarial harness.
/.github/                               @OWNER
/scripts/ci/                            @OWNER
/crates/vaultex-redteam/                @OWNER

# Supply chain: every dependency manifest and lockfile, container build recipes, the
# toolchain pin, advisory and vetting policy. Kept last so that a manifest anywhere in
# the tree (including inside a block above) goes to these owners.
Cargo.toml                              @OWNER
Cargo.lock                              @OWNER
package*.json                           @OWNER
Dockerfile*                             @OWNER
/rust-toolchain.toml                    @OWNER
/deny.toml                              @OWNER
/.cargo/                                @OWNER
/supply-chain/                          @OWNER
